From b02acac1b4efc7c23ed882199689bc690d37d48b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ashish Kumar Singh <ashishkmr472@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 15 Nov 2026 02:12:49 -0600
Subject: [PATCH] [XLA:GPU] FFI handlers that instantiate concurrently are
 instantiated together on the compile threads

A custom call's FFI instantiate stage ran inside thunk emission, one call at a time (CustomCallThunk::Create),
though the emitter's own kernels compile on the compile thread pool: a program of many Mosaic GPU kernels
compiled each serially (36 kernels, 16.3 s). A handler registered with
XLA_FFI_HANDLER_TRAITS_INSTANTIATE_CONCURRENTLY (ffi::Traits::kInstantiateConcurrently) states its instantiate
stage may run beside others; ThunkEmitter::InstantiateConcurrently instantiates every such call of the module
together before it emits thunks (KernelCompiler::RunConcurrently, the calling thread claiming tasks beside
the pool's), outside the LLVM options lock, and each call's thunk takes its state (CustomCallThunk::Create's
execution_state, CustomCallThunk::Instantiated the one instantiate). An instantiation's error is the compile's.
